# Paper-only branch. This file is the safety net that keeps the 2.6GB monorepo
# out of the Overleaf project.
#
# Why a whitelist and not a blacklist: this branch gets checked out into the same
# working directory as `main`, so every monorepo path (generated_art/ 634MB,
# godot_demo/ 141MB, ...) sits there as *untracked*. A single `git add -A` on this
# branch would stage all of it and the next push would ship it to Overleaf, which
# has no LFS. Ignoring everything by default makes that mistake impossible; new
# monorepo directories are covered automatically without editing this file.

# Ignore everything by default.
*

# Un-ignore only what LaTeX needs. Directories must be un-ignored before their
# contents, otherwise git never descends into them.
!.gitignore
!*.tex
!*.bib
!*.sty
!*.cls
!*.bst

!figures/
!figures/*.png
!figures/*.pdf
!figures/*.jpg
!figures/*.jpeg
!figures/*.eps

# Deliberately still ignored, even though they live under paper/ on main:
#   results/       scored JSON + analysis notes, not compiled by LaTeX
#   human_eval/    7.3MB of survey assets
#   figures/*.py   figure generators belong on main, not in the Overleaf project
#
# LaTeX build artifacts (*.aux, *.log, *.pdf at root, ...) need no rules:
# the leading `*` already covers them.
